From: Marius Balteanu <marius.balteanu@zitec.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:09:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Only render memberships in visible projects in the groups API
 (#44468).
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a Member.visible scope that restricts memberships to projects the
user is allowed to view members of, use it in the groups API template,
and switch users#show to the same scope so both endpoints share one
definition of a visible membership.

Patch by Jens Krämer (user:jkraemer).

git-svn-id: https://svn.redmine.org/redmine/trunk@25164 e93f8b46-1217-0410-a6f0-8f06a7374b81
(cherry picked from commit 39e799652b6d5108690e9d5c2f071bd85bad1130)
--- a/app/controllers/users_controller.rb
+++ b/app/controllers/users_controller.rb
@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@ class UsersController < ApplicationController
     end
 
     # show projects based on current user visibility
-    @memberships = @user.memberships.preload(:roles, :project).where(Project.visible_condition(User.current)).to_a
+    @memberships = @user.memberships.visible.preload(:roles, :project).to_a
 
     @issue_counts = {}
     @issue_counts[:assigned] = {
--- a/app/models/member.rb
+++ b/app/models/member.rb
@@ -33,6 +33,10 @@ class Member < ApplicationRecord
   scope :active, (lambda do
     joins(:principal).where(:users => {:status => Principal::STATUS_ACTIVE})
   end)
+  scope :visible, (lambda do |*args|
+    joins(:project).
+      where(Project.allowed_to_condition(args.shift || User.current, :view_members, *args))
+  end)
   # Sort by first role and principal
   scope :sorted, (lambda do
     includes(:member_roles, :roles, :principal).
--- a/app/views/groups/show.api.rsb
